<include>
  <!--
    Calls dialled from a registered manager extension (101, 102, ...).

    There is deliberately NO route from an extension to the Megafon trunk. A softphone or Linphone
    cannot dial an arbitrary external number: every external call is placed by the CRM through
    Calling's verified-destination policy (signed Staff Session, the Contact's own verified number,
    Contacts' voice permission), which originates the trunk leg over ESL and bridges the manager's
    extension in. A new number is called only after a Contact exists for it (Owner decision Q4,
    2026-11-11). This also closes the toll-fraud path through a registered or stolen extension.

    The former extension "user_outbound_megafon" (any 7/8/+7 number straight to
    sofia/gateway/megafon) was removed for that reason; modules/calling has a test that fails if any
    dialplan action bridges to the trunk again.
  -->

  <!-- Internal extension-to-extension calls (101 <-> 102, etc.) -->
  <extension name="user_internal">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^(1\d{2})$">
      <action application="bridge" data="user/$1"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
</include>
